tags: device-selection

A setting of a start, from the caller: the device that the node gives for an entry of
Container.devices.

The value is key=value lines, sorted by the bytes of the key, separated by a newline.
The key is the position of the entry in base 10. The value is the stable id of a device
of the node (the fact device-id, 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:39363aeedc67ec903b169ac2d0c5c11974a7eec39c49eb908032d806f331a46d). Example: 0=gpu-1.

With no setting, the node selects the devices. The node is bound: it gives that device,
or it refuses the start. When the instance wakes, the node gives the same device, or
the instance stays hibernated.

=== formal
class=setting
default=absent: the node selects the devices
name=device-selection
place=configuration
value=key=value lines sorted by key; the key is the position of an entry of Container.devices in base 10; the value is the value of the fact 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:39363aeedc67ec903b169ac2d0c5c11974a7eec39c49eb908032d806f331a46d of a device of the node
